Dataset Description

This project uses a synthetic dataset that simulates a digital comics reading platform. It contains information about users, reading activity, in-app purchases, refunds, and marketing campaigns.

The dataset consists of nine interconnected tables:

users — User IDs, registration dates, countries, device types, and marketing campaign IDs.

payments — Payment IDs, user IDs, purchased packages, transaction amounts, payment statuses, and completion dates.

refunds — Refund IDs, associated payment IDs, refunded amounts, and refund dates.

coin_packages — Virtual currency packages available for purchase.

comics — Comic IDs, titles, and genres.

episodes — Episode IDs and their associated comics.

reading_sessions — Reading session IDs, user IDs, episode IDs, session timestamps, and reading progress percentages.

episode_unlocks — Records of episodes unlocked by users.

campaigns — Marketing campaign IDs and advertising expenditures.

The tables are connected through primary and foreign keys, allowing information about users, transactions, reading behavior, and marketing activities to be analyzed together.

All data is artificially generated and does not represent real users or financial transactions.
